  "body": "Seen in the #1614 Hub run (770MX sim, 2026-11-13). The tool was already in the spindle. The program still ran `G53 G0 Z0` / `G30` / `T4 M6` / `G43 H4` / `G53 G0 Z0`. Hub's stored G30 Z sits about 0.9\" below the top of travel, so Z went up, dipped to the G30 height, and went straight back up (the #1596 re-lift) before the clearance move. It is safe (the G30 height was about 3\" above the part), but the user found it odd, and it is wasted motion.\n\n**Proposed fix:** when the stream's TOOL is the one already loaded, `tormach.cps` skips the G30 and M6 (keeping the G43 and the lift). Check how PathPilot treats an `M6` for the tool already in the spindle before relying on that. Note that at the program start the post cannot know what is loaded, so the first tool change of a program keeps its G30.\n\n**Done means:** a repeated tool number in the same program posts no second G30 / M6. That is pinned by a test, and the moved goldens are listed in the PR.\n\nRelated: #1614 (PR #1618), #1596.\n",
